msgctxt "#30027"
msgid "Live TV pause/rewind (timeshift)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30028"
msgid "Off (default): plain live stream, no pause/rewind, works immediately. Local: real pause/rewind buffered on this device via inputstream.ffmpegdirect (must be installed, or live playback fails) -- doesn't persist across a Kodi restart or follow you to another device. Server-side: pause/rewind/fast-forward buffered by Dispatcharr via the companion Timeshift Buffer plugin, shared across every device on the account -- needs a Dispatcharr admin account and the plugin's HTTP port reachable from this device. See docs/TIMESHIFT.md for the full comparison."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30035"
msgid "Recordings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30038"
msgid "Recordings/timers refresh interval (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30039"
msgid "How often to ask Kodi to re-check its recordings and timers list on its own, without waiting for a local action (like starting or deleting a recording from this Kodi) to prompt it. Without this, a change made another way -- from a different Kodi install sharing this Dispatcharr account, directly through Dispatcharr itself, or a recording finishing on its own with nothing local to react to it -- would only ever show up after restarting Kodi."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30040"
msgid "Enable real-time recording/timer updates (experimental)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30041"
msgid "Connects to Dispatcharr's own real-time update feed so changes (new/edited recordings and timers) show up in Kodi immediately instead of waiting for the refresh interval above, which still runs as a fallback. Experimental: newer, less-tested networking code -- leave off if unsure. Needs a Kodi restart to take effect; Kodi will prompt you when you save."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30049"
msgid "Recurring timer: manual timezone offset from UTC (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30050"
msgid "Only used when the timezone setting above is \"Manual\". Set to Dispatcharr's configured system timezone's CURRENT offset from UTC in minutes (e.g. -300 for US Central Daylight Time) -- if that zone observes daylight saving, update this by 60 minutes yourself twice a year, or a recurring timer will fire an hour off. Leave at 0 for UTC. Only affects recurring (day-of-week) timers. See docs/RECURRING_RULES.md for the full explanation."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30051"
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30052"
msgid "Local (this device)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30053"
msgid "Server-side (Dispatcharr plugin)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30054"
msgid "Recording padding: start early (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30055"
msgid "Mirrors Dispatcharr's own global recording padding (Settings -> DVR) -- there's no per-timer equivalent, so this changes it for every EPG-based recording at once. Doesn't affect recurring (day-of-week) timers. Kept in sync with Dispatcharr's real value on every Kodi restart. Pushing a change here needs a Dispatcharr admin account; with a lesser account it fails silently (logged to kodi.log, nothing shown in the UI). See docs/RECORDINGS.md for details."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30056"
msgid "Recording padding: stop late (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30057"
msgid "The end-of-recording counterpart to the start-padding setting above -- see its help text for the full explanation (global-only, EPG-based recordings only, kept in sync with Dispatcharr's real value on restart)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30058"
msgid "Dispatcharr's configured timezone (for reference)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30059"
msgid "Read-only: Dispatcharr's own configured system timezone (IANA name, e.g. \"America/Chicago\"), kept in sync on every restart. Mainly useful as a reference when your zone isn't in the dropdown below and you need to fall back to manual offset entry."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30060"
msgid "Recurring timer: timezone"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30061"
msgid "Only affects recurring (day-of-week) timers. Pick the zone matching Dispatcharr's own configured system timezone (shown above) and this addon computes the correct UTC offset automatically, including daylight saving. Auto-selected on every restart when your zone is in this list. If it isn't, choose \"Manual\" and use the offset setting below instead. See docs/RECURRING_RULES.md for details."
msgstr ""

